# Frontend

## neel.js (the shim)
- Plain ES2020, no build step, no dependencies, works as a classic `<script>` and
  when imported from a module.
- Placeholders substituted at compile time by `src/neel/frontend.nim` use the form
  `__NEEL_TOKEN__`, `__NEEL_WINDOW_ID__`, `__NEEL_EXPOSED__`. Do not rename them
  without updating `frontend.nim`.
- Wire format is defined in `PLAN.md` "Protocol reference": `call` / `ret` / `err`
  with optional `id`. Keep the shim symmetric with the Nim side.
- `neel.<name>(...)` returns a Promise; `neel.<name>.send(...)` is fire-and-forget.
  `neel.expose(fn)` / `neel.expose({name: fn})` registers Nim-callable functions;
  lookup falls back to `window[name]`.
- Reject with an `Error` whose `name` is the Nim exception kind and `message` is the
  Nim message, so `catch (e) { e.name === "ValueError" }` works.

## Examples
- Use absolute asset paths (`/main.js`, `/style.css`); the server serves the web
  folder at `/`.
- Never assign untrusted strings to `innerHTML`; use `textContent`.
- Prefer self-contained assets over CDN links so release builds embed everything.

```js
// good
const name = await neel.filePicker(dir);
out.textContent = name;

// fire-and-forget
neel.log.send("clicked");
```
